  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Function notation, composite and inverse functions form a core Extended-tier topic.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Functions",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( f(x) \\) gives the output for an input \\( x \\). The composite \\( fg(x)=f(g(x)) \\) is applied inside-out; the inverse \\( f^{-1} \\) reverses \\( f \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Notation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f(x) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Composite",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( fg(x) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Inverse",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f^{-1}(x) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Domain",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "valid inputs",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>If \\( f(x)=2x+3 \\), find \\( f^{-1}(x) \\).</p>\\[ f^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-3}{2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 9.B — Composite and inverse",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Given \\(f(x)=2x+3\\) and \\(g(x)=x^{2}\\), find (a) \\(fg(3)\\), (b) \\(f^{-1}(x)\\).</p><p>(a) \\(fg(3)=f(9)=2(9)+3=21\\).</p><p>(b) Let \\(y=2x+3\\). Swap and solve: \\(x=\\dfrac{y-3}{2}\\). So \\(f^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{x-3}{2}\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "\\(h(x)=\\dfrac{3x-1}{2}\\). Find \\(h^{-1}(4)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(y=\\dfrac{3x-1}{2}\\Rightarrow2y=3x-1\\Rightarrow x=\\dfrac{2y+1}{3}\\). So \\(h^{-1}(x)=\\dfrac{2x+1}{3}\\) and \\(h^{-1}(4)=\\dfrac{9}{3}=3\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
